This is a targeted record of the queries that materially informed the audit, not an invented complete search-engine transcript. Searches also followed citations and exact titles from the supplied ledgers, but the conclusions were checked against primary sources. Secondary search hits were not used as theorem authorities.

**Negative search result:** no inspected source was found stating the exact fixed-cut rank-threshold formula. This establishes only that the present search did not locate one. The formal result remains a minor corollary with unresolved exact priority. The search did locate strong antecedents for the large majority of the surrounding theory. No theorem is called novel merely because an equivalent wording was absent from returned results.
